The closest file to the run wins a key, which is why the order matters: a
nested layer putting the sandbox back is the fix, and reporting it anyway
would be a finding against a configuration that never applied.

The root still answers for a run started there, so this fixture keeps the
root's sandbox bounded too and nothing is left to report.

>>> .codex/config.toml
approval_policy = "never"
sandbox_mode = "read-only"
>>> service/.codex/config.toml
sandbox_mode = "workspace-write"
approval_policy = "on-request"
